1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,380
Chai Corner now has two
outlets, and eight people.

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:05,553
But nobody is sure who does what.

3
00:00:06,103 --> 00:00:10,460
At the bus stand, two people make
tea, and nobody washes the cups.

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:14,791
Both outlets buy milk on the same
day, so half of it goes sour.

5
00:00:15,091 --> 00:00:17,758
And every small question
still goes to Ravi.

6
00:00:18,408 --> 00:00:20,328
Ravi doesn't need more people.

7
00:00:20,328 --> 00:00:21,806
He needs a structure.

8
00:00:22,506 --> 00:00:24,394
That night, Kabir checks the books.

9
00:00:24,744 --> 00:00:25,987
Milk bought twice.

10
00:00:25,987 --> 00:00:28,016
Cups run out at the bus stand.

11
00:00:28,016 --> 00:00:29,746
The money tells the story.

12
00:00:30,096 --> 00:00:32,591
Every problem has the same cause.

13
00:00:32,591 --> 00:00:34,236
Nobody owns the job.

14
00:00:34,886 --> 00:00:36,668
The fix is organizing.

15
00:00:36,968 --> 00:00:41,550
Organizing means arranging people
and resources, so the plan gets done.

16
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:43,904
It gives everyone a clear role.

17
00:00:43,904 --> 00:00:45,528
That is, what they do.

18
00:00:45,878 --> 00:00:47,026
Clear authority.

19
00:00:47,026 --> 00:00:49,145
That is, the power to decide.

20
00:00:49,495 --> 00:00:50,714
And a clear boss.

21
00:00:50,714 --> 00:00:52,680
That is, who reports to whom.

22
00:00:53,330 --> 00:00:55,644
Ravi organizes in five steps.

23
00:00:55,994 --> 00:00:56,894
One.

24
00:00:56,494 --> 00:00:57,896
List the activities.

25
00:00:57,896 --> 00:01:01,416
Boil tea, serve, take
cash, wash cups, buy milk.

26
00:01:01,766 --> 00:01:02,666
Two.

27
00:01:02,332 --> 00:01:03,352
Group them.

28
00:01:03,352 --> 00:01:05,281
Similar jobs go together.

29
00:01:05,631 --> 00:01:06,531
Three.

30
00:01:06,242 --> 00:01:08,047
Give each group an owner.

31
00:01:08,047 --> 00:01:09,691
Asha leads the kitchen.

32
00:01:09,691 --> 00:01:11,235
Kabir runs the money.

33
00:01:11,585 --> 00:01:12,485
Four.

34
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:13,582
Delegate authority.

35
00:01:13,582 --> 00:01:16,090
That means handing some power down.

36
00:01:16,090 --> 00:01:18,438
Asha can now order milk herself.

37
00:01:18,788 --> 00:01:19,688
And five.

38
00:01:19,555 --> 00:01:22,841
Link the groups to Ravi,
so they work as one team.

39
00:01:23,491 --> 00:01:26,051
That second step has a special name.

40
00:01:26,051 --> 00:01:27,201
Departmentation.

41
00:01:27,551 --> 00:01:30,460
It means grouping
activities into departments.

42
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:32,360
There are five common ways.

43
00:01:32,710 --> 00:01:33,621
Functional.

44
00:01:33,621 --> 00:01:34,766
Group by job.

45
00:01:34,766 --> 00:01:36,929
Kitchen, cash, and counter.

46
00:01:37,279 --> 00:01:38,179
Territorial.

47
00:01:38,167 --> 00:01:39,320
Group by place.

48
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:41,780
The first stall, and the bus stand.

49
00:01:42,130 --> 00:01:43,030
Product.

50
00:01:42,823 --> 00:01:44,482
Group by what you sell.

51
00:01:44,482 --> 00:01:45,828
Chai, and snacks.

52
00:01:46,178 --> 00:01:47,078
Customer.

53
00:01:46,961 --> 00:01:48,713
Group by who you serve.

54
00:01:48,713 --> 00:01:52,094
Walk-in buyers, and bulk
orders from nearby shops.

55
00:01:52,444 --> 00:01:53,344
And process.

56
00:01:53,322 --> 00:01:55,332
Group by the steps of the work.

57
00:01:55,332 --> 00:01:56,953
Boil, brew, and serve.

58
00:01:57,603 --> 00:01:59,480
No single way is best.

59
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:00,822
Ravi mixes two.

60
00:02:01,172 --> 00:02:02,157
Places first.

61
00:02:02,157 --> 00:02:04,589
The first stall, and the bus stand.

62
00:02:04,589 --> 00:02:06,374
Then jobs inside each one.

63
00:02:06,724 --> 00:02:10,096
Now a small question at the
bus stand stops with Meena.

64
00:02:10,746 --> 00:02:14,631
You'll find these departments
in big organizations everywhere.

65
00:02:14,981 --> 00:02:15,881
Functional.

66
00:02:15,859 --> 00:02:19,565
A company has marketing,
finance, and human resources.

67
00:02:19,915 --> 00:02:20,815
Territorial.

68
00:02:20,794 --> 00:02:23,642
A bank runs a north zone and a south zone.

69
00:02:23,992 --> 00:02:24,892
Product.

70
00:02:24,698 --> 00:02:28,643
A vehicle maker has one team
for cars, and one for trucks.

71
00:02:28,993 --> 00:02:29,893
Customer.

72
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:33,785
A bank serves home buyers and
businesses through separate teams.

73
00:02:34,135 --> 00:02:35,035
Process.

74
00:02:34,802 --> 00:02:38,260
A garment factory runs cutting,
stitching, and packing.

75
00:02:38,910 --> 00:02:40,864
But departments come with a catch.

76
00:02:41,214 --> 00:02:42,365
The good side.

77
00:02:42,365 --> 00:02:45,491
Clear roles, expert
teams, and fewer mix-ups.

78
00:02:45,841 --> 00:02:46,969
The hard side.

79
00:02:46,969 --> 00:02:50,404
Each department can start
to think only about itself.

80
00:02:50,754 --> 00:02:52,287
People call these silos.

81
00:02:52,287 --> 00:02:56,243
The kitchen blames the counter,
and the counter blames the kitchen.

82
00:02:56,593 --> 00:03:00,341
Back in 1916, Henri Fayol
suggested a gangplank.

83
00:03:00,341 --> 00:03:04,796
People on the same level talk
directly, across departments.

84
00:03:05,146 --> 00:03:06,225
So the lesson.

85
00:03:06,225 --> 00:03:09,108
Build departments, but
keep the bridges open.

86
00:03:09,758 --> 00:03:10,723
Quick check.

87
00:03:10,723 --> 00:03:14,923
Ravi makes one team for walk-in
buyers, and one for bulk orders.

88
00:03:14,923 --> 00:03:16,356
Which type is this?

89
00:03:18,256 --> 00:03:19,156
Customer!

90
00:03:18,947 --> 00:03:21,426
The teams are grouped by who they serve.

91
00:03:22,026 --> 00:03:23,035
So, remember.

92
00:03:23,335 --> 00:03:27,192
Organizing gives everyone a
clear role, authority, and boss.

93
00:03:27,542 --> 00:03:31,780
Departments can be built by function,
territory, product, customer, or

94
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:32,680
process.

95
00:03:32,791 --> 00:03:35,700
And keep bridges between
them, so they work as one.

96
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:37,845
Next time, staffing.

97
00:03:37,845 --> 00:03:41,268
How Ravi finds, hires and
trains the right people.
